 u.instructure.com/api/v1/courses/35044/files/13505320" data-api-returntype
 ="File">Discussions Transcript</a></span></p>\n<p><span style="color: #000
 000\;">You will have the opportunity in upcoming lessons to study many tal
 ks and messages taught by President Oaks. In this unit\, you have learned 
 more about his calling and his biography. Now we will consider this questi
 on together: <em>In what ways is his life a sermon?</em> Follow the prompt
 s below to share lessons you learned from his life experience.</span></p>
 \n<p><span style="color: #000000\;">For this discussion\, you will make tw
 o separate posts:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Post 1\, </strong>due by T
 uesday: Write <span style="text-decoration: underline\;">two</span> solid 
 paragraphs (4–6 sentences each)\n<ul>\n<li><span style="color: #000000\;
 ">Each paragraph should very briefly mention one particular life theme or 
 event from President Oaks's life (you do not need to repeat its details)\,
 </span></li>\n<li><span style="color: #000000\;">Then explain what princip
 les you learned\, and </span></li>\n<li><span style="color: #000000\;">Com
 ment on how <em>you</em> can apply that example in your own life and circu
 mstances.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><span style="color: #000000\;"><s
 trong>Post 2\, </strong>due by Wednesday: After reading 5+ of your peers' 
 posts\, make a separate\, one-paragraph <em>Summary + Response</em> post. 
 What themes and additional ideas stood out to you in the examples and thou
 ghts they shared?</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style="color: #000000\;">Fu
 ll points will be rewarded for one initial post plus a later <em>Summary +
  Response</em> post\, with each demonstrating considered engagement relate
 d to the lesson material.</span></p>\n<p><span style="color: #000000\;"><s
 trong>Rubric:</strong> You will earn up to 6 points for the content and re
 quirements of your initial post (each paragraph: event\, principle\, appli
 cation) and 4 points for your thoughtful summary and response to the group
  discussion. To see the complete rubric\, click on the three dots in the t
 op right corner of this page. Then click "Show Rubric."</span></p>\n<p cla
